Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.35,0:00:04.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Kimbly!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.77,0:00:05.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey there.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.96,0:00:11.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.87,0:00:14.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to take revenge for what you did to Greed-san and my friends!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.74,0:00:17.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Kimbly-san, \Nwhat are you doing here?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.80,0:00:21.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It shouldn't be that unusual, \Nconsidering I {\i1}am{\i0} a State Alchemist, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.54,0:00:24.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You sold us out and returned to the military! You're the worst!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.98,0:00:28.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you sure you want to let her kill me like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.09,0:00:31.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Martel-san, please stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.71,0:00:35.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you doing?! \NLet go! Let go of me!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.22,0:00:36.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.22,0:00:36.76,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,Please stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.76,0:00:38.88,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,{\pos(360,470)}Let go of me already!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.76,0:00:40.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You should make for some fine fireworks.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.88,0:00:40.77,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,Martel-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.09,0:00:42.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let go of me!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.77,0:00:48.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Kimbly-san, what are you doing to that man?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.00,0:00:50.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am, first and foremost, a soldier.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.27,0:00:52.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no reason why I should \Nbear the blame of some hooligan.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.57,0:00:57.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Martel-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.91,0:01:12.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything \Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.64,0:01:17.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to obtain anything, \Nsomething of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.91,0:01:22.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is alchemy's \NLaw of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.64,0:01:28.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that \Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.62,0:03:10.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And here I was hoping to see a really exciting explosion...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.11,0:03:13.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But thanks to your interference...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.21,0:03:22.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please don't lay a finger \Non Martel-san.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.86,0:03:25.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By Martel, do you \Nmean this snake here?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.81,0:03:27.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Martel-san is a person!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.59,0:03:29.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wasn't aware of that.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.91,0:03:31.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,These guys are Chimeras.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.89,0:03:34.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They aren't even \Nfull-fledged life forms!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.06,0:03:35.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Kind of like you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.29,0:03:38.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You get away from Martel-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.82,0:03:42.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not giving you \Nthe chance to transmute!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.84,0:03:48.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.33,0:03:53.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.94,0:04:00.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,To think that you'd be deliberately providing me with ingredients...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.69,0:04:20.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Martel-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.77,0:04:27.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, you monster...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.55,0:04:35.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.51,0:04:41.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He, like his brother, \Nis under my jurisdiction.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.27,0:04:45.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you have any problems with him, you can file a written complaint.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.41,0:04:50.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mark my words, I'm going to blow up that suit of armor.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.18,0:04:53.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're going to the \Nfrontlines yourself, Führer?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.48,0:04:57.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I won't let Liore \Nbecome another Ishbal.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.01,0:04:59.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Unless we bring an end to this quickly, with a minimum of casualties...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.93,0:05:02.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Y-Yes, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.20,0:05:05.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I want you to take over \Nas acting Führer.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.26,0:05:07.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Y-You want {\i1}me{\i0} to?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.60,0:05:08.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't let me down.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.09,0:05:10.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.92,0:05:23.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Acting Führer! Acting Führer!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.17,0:05:27.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, and sorry, but could you send something to my wife for me?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.15,0:05:29.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She gets lonely \Nall alone at home.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.03,0:05:30.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All right...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.25,0:05:31.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm counting on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.27,0:05:34.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.49,0:05:38.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yet another city must fall...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.99,0:05:41.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,for those who seek \Nthe Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.74,0:05:52.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you've come this far, then you must know what my objective is.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.87,0:05:53.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.94,0:05:57.87,Dialogue,,20,20,0,,You must be thinking of doing something foolish, \Nlike creating a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.96,0:06:00.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I won't let you get in my way.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.56,0:06:03.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.46,0:06:07.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's something I have to ask you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.47,0:06:10.87,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Four years ago, back in Central, \Ndid you see a Chimera that looked like a dog?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.87,0:06:13.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I sent it back to God.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.01,0:06:14.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why would you do that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.73,0:06:17.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What else would you \Nhave had me do?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.80,0:06:21.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's not the kind of thing \Nthat we should be deciding!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.41,0:06:24.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that all you have to say?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.40,0:06:26.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you plan on wiping out Rose and the other people of this city
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.55,0:06:29.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,with that same self-serving logic?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.93,0:06:31.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You know Rose?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.14,0:06:39.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to open your eyes!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.09,0:06:58.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.02,0:07:02.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't you know? \NYou're an alchemist, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.25,0:07:04.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm an alchemist?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.22,0:07:05.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alchemy is comprised of
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.82,0:07:08.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the three steps of comprehension, decomposition, and reconstruction.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.82,0:07:11.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You unconsciously read your \Nopponent's metallic composition
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.93,0:07:15.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and then adjust your own technique to destroy it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.87,0:07:19.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why I've been replacing the metal of my Automail
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.04,0:07:23.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,with other metals besides steel.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.55,0:07:25.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So that's it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.38,0:07:28.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Of course, rapidly swapping around the metal in my Automail
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.74,0:07:31.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is messing up its \Ndelicate adjustments,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.70,0:07:33.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so I'm going to \Nput you down quick!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.90,0:07:46.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You dimwit!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.66,0:07:50.00,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Once you use the lives of this town's people \Nto make your Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.00,0:07:53.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it will then be {\i1}your{\i0} turn to have vengeance taken against you!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.07,0:07:58.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Have you forgotten? \NI can also destroy living flesh.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.87,0:08:05.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Homunculi?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.76,0:08:07.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Call me Lust, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.67,0:08:09.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm Gluttony!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.62,0:08:14.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You understand why we're telling you our names, right, Fullmetal Boy?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.10,0:08:17.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, you mean that today, we'll be saying good-bye.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.11,0:08:37.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, that was hot!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.09,0:08:39.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't kill us off so casually, if you don't mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.81,0:08:41.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Like you did to Greed.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.83,0:08:48.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And here we were protecting you,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.09,0:08:50.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,scarred man of Ishbal.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.53,0:08:53.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am your enemy, am I not?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.21,0:08:56.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you're going to create a Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.30,0:08:58.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,then we will protect you.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.69,0:09:01.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We won't let the boy interfere, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.13,0:09:03.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you recognize this?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.39,0:09:06.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It is something you gave my brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.65,0:09:09.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.37,0:09:10.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Remember!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.07,0:09:17.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lust?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.02,0:09:19.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lust!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.69,0:09:25.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I hate you! I hate you all!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.72,0:09:35.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the story between \Nyou and that homunculus?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.93,0:09:37.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's none of your business!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.69,0:09:41.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.54,0:09:44.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose... and Lyra as well?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.02,0:09:47.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Please, listen to what \Nthat man has to say, Ed."
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.81,0:09:51.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's what Rose-san \Napparently wants to tell you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.64,0:09:55.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose, you can't talk?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.03,0:10:03.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Keep it as a good-luck charm
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.67,0:10:06.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so that even when I'm gone, you won't forget about me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.19,0:10:14.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Back when Ishbal was still peaceful,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.32,0:10:16.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I had an older brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.04,0:10:21.12,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,An intelligent brother, whom I was proud of \Nand whom was respected by everyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.29,0:10:24.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My brother had a beautiful girlfriend.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.15,0:10:28.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She fell ill,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.80,0:10:31.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and soon after, she was called home to Ishbala.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.32,0:10:41.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, what are you searching for?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.36,0:10:43.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Grand Art.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.25,0:10:45.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a hallowed endeavor that can bring all people back to life.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.70,0:10:49.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's what those people from Central recently tried to promulgate here—
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.68,0:10:51.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,what they called alchemy—isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.25,0:10:54.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They say that \Nwithin the Grand Art,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.25,0:10:56.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,there is a technique that \Nbrings people back to life.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.60,0:10:59.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I see...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.28,0:11:01.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So that's it. That explains it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.91,0:11:12.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother! Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.34,0:11:23.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My brother defied the teachings of Ishbala in order to bring her back to life.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.90,0:11:25.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He lost part of his body.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.89,0:11:29.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And yet, she still \Nhad not come back.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.91,0:11:33.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My brother was cast out.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.13,0:11:36.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Grand Art was the greatest abomination in Ishbal, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.36,0:11:40.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, did my brother succeed after all?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.27,0:11:43.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That woman named Lust...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.72,0:11:46.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you know how \Nhomunculi are born?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.26,0:11:50.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,People conduct human transmutation and fail.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.76,0:11:53.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The botched product that is born at that time is a homunculus.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.81,0:11:58.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come to mention it, I heard about that from Dante-san as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.49,0:12:01.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She said she once committed human transmutation
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.60,0:12:03.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and had created a homunculus.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.86,0:12:07.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That could have been Greed.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.31,0:12:10.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But they shouldn't be able to survive very long as they are.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.60,0:12:14.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Someone is gathering up \Nhomunculi like Lust and Envy,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.49,0:12:16.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,giving them multiple lives, and controlling them.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.96,0:12:19.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then Lust is the one \Nmy brother created?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.51,0:12:21.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She doesn't have a soul.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.98,0:12:25.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She's just a monster that \Nhas the same appearance.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.02,0:12:33.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lust was affected by \Nthis good-luck charm.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.79,0:12:37.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Homunculi have a weakness when \Nit comes to the remains of the person
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.31,0:12:40.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,who was the basis of their human transmutation.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.86,0:12:47.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Soon after my brother departed,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.48,0:12:50.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,we were invaded for no reason.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.79,0:12:55.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We were angered by the \Nsudden attack and rose up.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.18,0:13:00.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And so, a long conflict began.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.21,0:13:03.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've learned a way to create a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.42,0:13:05.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.56,0:13:07.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we were to possess its power,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.38,0:13:09.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,we could save Ishbal \Nfrom its crisis.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.94,0:13:12.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In the middle of the war,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.70,0:13:16.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,nobody rebuked \Nmy brother for returning.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.23,0:13:20.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, just as my brother was about to complete the Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.05,0:13:22.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,he suddenly renounced his research.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.16,0:13:28.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I now know the reason why.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.78,0:13:32.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I also heard the story, \Nfrom an outcast in Kishua.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.75,0:13:34.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It takes a large number \Nof human lives
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.46,0:13:37.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,to create a Philosopher's Stone using the Grand Art as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.71,0:13:39.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.24,0:13:41.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It probably takes so many lives
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.46,0:13:44.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that it would mean the destruction of a whole town, or a whole people.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.51,0:13:50.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Unless the frustration, malice, \Nand anger released at that time
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.47,0:13:53.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,all blend together,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.43,0:13:55.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,a Philosopher's Stone \Ncannot be formed.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.92,0:13:59.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to save Ishbal, \Nwe needed a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.50,0:14:03.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, for that to happen,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.00,0:14:06.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ishbal would have to be destroyed.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.12,0:14:15.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am the State Alchemist in charge of the extermination of this district.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.90,0:14:17.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,State Alchemist?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.71,0:14:19.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No more, please!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.17,0:14:21.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We have been driven from our land, \Nand we are fleeing.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.92,0:14:23.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Isn't that enough?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.69,0:14:26.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was just told to exterminate you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.53,0:14:32.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am to stamp out every last one of you who has eyes and skin of a different color.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.22,0:14:33.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.27,0:14:34.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who knows?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.32,0:14:46.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A light bulb just \Nwent off in my head.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.00,0:14:49.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I think I'll blow up your body, a little bit at a time.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.57,0:14:53.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,First, I'll turn your skin \Ninto an explosive.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.90,0:15:00.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whoops...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.08,0:15:02.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Next will be this arm.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.01,0:15:09.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now then, next will be...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.49,0:15:16.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That body of yours looks like a transmutation circle.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.36,0:15:19.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I didn't know there were any alchemists in Ishbal.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.78,0:15:24.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, we have these \Ntransmutation amplifiers.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.12,0:15:41.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel Grand!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.76,0:16:00.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What the?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.14,0:16:03.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.52,0:16:04.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.79,0:16:14.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I commit the lives of our people \Nwithin my body...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.18,0:16:17.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.58,0:16:20.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No! Brother, why did you do this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.46,0:16:23.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is power within that arm.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.00,0:16:27.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If I had not done this, \Nyou would be dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.51,0:16:30.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother... Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.64,0:16:34.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have done something \Nthat cannot be forgiven.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.75,0:16:39.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You... liked her, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.60,0:16:41.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Forgive me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.16,0:16:46.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am going on ahead... to see her, first...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.38,0:17:05.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your brother was trying to transmute \Na Philosopher's Stone inside his own body.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.22,0:17:09.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He took the lives of the dying Ishbalan people
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.80,0:17:12.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and entrusted them to you, together with his own arm.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.78,0:17:15.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Philosopher's Stone itself possesses power.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.30,0:17:19.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's how I managed to hold on to my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.05,0:17:22.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That arm itself is an unfinished Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.61,0:17:25.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why it reacts \Nwith red stones.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.06,0:17:29.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It will take even more lives \Nto complete it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.65,0:17:33.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Which is why you're setting Rose up \Nto be some charismatic leader
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.38,0:17:35.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and manipulating \Nthe people of Liore?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.10,0:17:36.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold on!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.69,0:17:40.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Scar-san is not going to \Nsacrifice the people of Liore.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.24,0:17:43.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lyra, what are you \Neven doing here?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.36,0:17:45.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After Dante-san passed away,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.84,0:17:48.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I searched for a place where \NI could make my alchemy useful.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.72,0:17:52.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And then I learned \Nof Scar-san's plans.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.62,0:17:55.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just before the fighting begins,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.63,0:17:58.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the people are going to flee through an underground passageway
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.62,0:18:00.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that has been made \Nunder the old church.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.25,0:18:03.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And then, the soldiers who have been lured into the city will be...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.73,0:18:14.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That means there will \Nstill be casualties!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.81,0:18:17.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Besides, how is it \Nall right to kill soldi—
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.04,0:18:35.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you know what \Nthey've done in this town?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.70,0:18:38.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What did the military do to Rose?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.18,0:18:40.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She was taken into \Nthe military's custody,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.76,0:18:43.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and when she came home, she had lost her speech.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.34,0:18:48.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Would you still ask us to forgive the military?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.87,0:18:57.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Martel-san, where are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.95,0:19:02.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is a problem. \NI want to go pick up Brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.70,0:19:05.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Havoc-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.79,0:19:09.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the matter? \NDon't tell me there's an attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.08,0:19:13.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't know what's going on, \Nbut I heard that the Führer has arrived.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.70,0:19:28.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It pleases me that the Führer himself would call for someone such as myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.52,0:19:32.94,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,There is a matter of some secrecy that \NI would like you two to lend me a hand with.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.94,0:19:39.26,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Lt. Col. Kimbly, I want you to take the lead of Tucker-kun's Chimeras and infiltrate the city.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.26,0:19:44.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I see, so you want us to run wild \Nand provoke them into attacking?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.41,0:19:47.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The same trick that we used in the fighting at Ishbal.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.45,0:19:50.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But even if we don't \Ngo to all that trouble...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.87,0:19:54.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We will only act in order \Nto restore peace.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.37,0:19:57.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If they're the ones who start it, \Nwe can say we're fighting for a just cause.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.39,0:20:03.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Also, there is still one \NState Alchemist in Liore, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.25,0:20:04.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward Elric?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.49,0:20:09.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He has probably been killed. Find his body for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.60,0:20:12.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That will make our cause \Neven more just.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.35,0:20:16.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if I don't find his corpse, \NI will see to it that he becomes one.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.76,0:20:20.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A shame that \Nwe had to lose him.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.86,0:20:25.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I won't let you do it!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.50,0:20:28.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I won't let you do the same thing you did to Ishbal, nor will I let you kill Ed!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.98,0:20:31.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come on, you're going to withdraw those orders!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.08,0:20:32.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Or else...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.22,0:20:48.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your swift movements \Nwill not work against me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.61,0:20:51.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have the Mightiest Eye, you see.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.50,0:20:59.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Ed! Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.47,0:21:05.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.61,0:21:06.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Martel-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.83,0:21:08.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al, listen to me, and tell Ed, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.87,0:21:10.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whatever, just get inside me!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.08,0:21:16.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al, listen...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.73,0:21:41.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you okay, Alphonse-kun?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.38,0:21:45.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have executed the Chimera that appeared to be threatening you.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.28,0:23:40.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.00,0:23:43.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 41: "Holy Mother"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.02,0:23:45.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I hear it—that voice...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.44,0:23:50.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That familiar voice, that was supposed to have been lost a long time ago...
